    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the \"reject duplicate email \u2192 409\" rule for `POST /api/owners`, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `RequireUniqueTelephone` pattern):\n\n**New files:**\n- `RequireUniqueEmail.java` \u2014 a pipeline step that reads the validated `OwnerFieldsDto`, and if it carries a (non-blank) email, compares its trimmed/lower-cased form against every existing owner's email, throwing a checked `DuplicateEmailException` on a match. Email is optional, so a request without one is never a conflict.\n- `DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`).\n- `DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `409 Conflict` with a `ProblemDetail`, matching the telephone handler.\n- `.../escalation/...DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Wiring:**\n- Inserted a `uniqueEmail` step into `owners.POST.yml` right after the telephone-uniqueness check, under the same `govern: [ transaction ]` governance, chaining `unique \u2192 uniqueEmail \u2192 household`.\n\nComparison uses lower-cased values on both sides (existing owner emails are stored lower-cased by `ApplyOwner`; incoming email is lower-cased by `RequireOwnerFields`), satisfying \"lower-cased email already used by any other owner.\"\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` passes and the build is green.",
